# Secrets and credentials

- Do not commit `.env`, `.env.bak`, `.env.backup*`, `.env.clean`, `.env.local`, or any file containing real secrets.
- Only `.env.example` at repo root may be tracked, with placeholders only.
- JWT tokens are short-lived; refresh flows live in `core/auth.py`. Never hardcode tokens.
- Treat Discord webhook URLs as secrets; keep them in environment / secret store, not source.
- Account IDs are sensitive: use `<account_num>` in docs and PRs; avoid logging or pasting real IDs.
- If `pre-commit` runs `gitleaks`, keep it enabled as a last line of defense. Install hooks with `pre-commit install`.
